# How to Use: Update Media Script

This script automatically scans your litter folders on your computer and safely adds any newly dropped photos or videos directly into `data.js`. 

## What it does:
* It checks all images and videos in your litter folders in `assets/Listings/`.
* If it finds any files that are missing from `data.js`, it will:
   * Figure out if it's an image or a video.
   * Auto-generate the label by searching for a puppy name in the filename (e.g., `wendy1.png` becomes `Wendy (Girl)`).
   * Safely append all the new files into `data.js`.

---

## Instructions

1. Drop your new photos and videos into their respective litter folders inside `assets/Listings/`.
2. Open **PowerShell** and navigate to your `OrchardPups` folder.

3. **(Recommended) Test Run**: Run this command first. It will print out a list of all the files it plans to add without actually making any changes:
   ```powershell
   .\Automation_Scripts\Update-Media.ps1 -DryRun
   ```

4. **Real Run**: When everything looks correct in the test run, run this command to safely add them to the website:
   ```powershell
   .\Automation_Scripts\Update-Media.ps1
   ```

> [!NOTE]
> Depending on your computer's security settings, you might get a red error saying scripts are disabled. If so, use this bypass command instead:
> `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\Automation_Scripts\Update-Media.ps1`
